<title>PHILIPPINES: Fil-Estate unit eyes condominium in Subic.</title>
<headline>Fil-Estate unit eyes condominium in Subic.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fil-Estate Properties Inc (FEPI), a wholly-owned subsidiary of Fil-Estate Land Inc, is planning to build residential condominiums inside the Subic freeport area, the parent company said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;FEPI has entered into a revised deed of partial assignment of leasehold rights with Subic Bay Waterfront Development Corp ... The portion assigned to FEPI is, under the master plan, reserved for the construction of condominium residential buildings,&quot; vice president Frederico Alquiros told the Securities and Exchange Commission.</p>
<p>The contract is expected to be approved by the Subic Bay Metropolitan Authority.</p>
<p>No other details were available.</p>
<p>- Manila newsroom 63 2 8418938 Fax 8176267</p>
</text>
